- [will_said + observed] QEXO MERGED; WINDOWS + DISK-GATE FIXES: Will reported a failing doctor test on Windows. Diagnosis: the test encodes Unix mode semantics as universal, and stale_lock judged liveness by /proc/{pid} (never exists on Windows) — doctor --fix there would delete a live lock. Fix: per-platform pid_alive (ambiguity reads ALIVE); gates passed; Windows runtime rests on Will's re-run. DISK-GATE: merged qexo read RED at ~809 GB used on a 3.6 TB volume with 2.7 TB free — absolute thresholds calibrated to the Muse VM quota. Fix: probe returns raw bytes and judges nothing; thresholds are field lines in the state.phext config record; live repro GREEN. STACKED-PR FLAW NAMED: a stacked PR whose base is not the main branch traps the natural merge; future bases stay exo.

