- [will_said] MULTIVERSE ADDRESSING RULED (Will, 11:24): a phext with no 0x02 bytes is implicitly a single-universe phext — the degenerate case; a chain is a multiverse, each member a universe indexed from 1; addressing is $N:<address>, the 1: prefix may be omitted. This supersedes the flag that a chain-free file parses as one unclosed chain: it is a COMPLETE single universe. Implemented on the v0.6 branch, Emise's review APPROVE.
