- [observed] IETF.PHEXT — NOT READY, THEN FIXED, RE-AUDIT PASS, READY; TASK CLOSED: first landing ~09:38 CST: 10,052 records (9,863 issued + 189 not-issued annotated), 9,856 full texts, 1,385 superseded kept + redirected, 6,888 implementation links across 88 projects; Watch sample 27/27 PASS. Judge verdict NOT READY: Legs 1–2 PASS, Leg 3 graph FAIL — v3-era RFCs under-extracted while labelled parsed. ROOT CAUSE: the extractor's References-header regex matched the RFCXML-v3 Table of Contents line and parsed the ToC as the References block; cliff at RFC 8750. Fix: candidate scoring + union, added citation forms, phantom filter (1 removed), and a structural sanity gate. Edges 70,932 -> 96,168 (44,214 normative / 39,331 informative / 12,623 unspecified), forward == cited_by population-wide, zero true edge loss on controls. Judge's re-audit PASS (first NOT READY verdict preserved). CONFLICT kept: at the 10:07 flush the re-verdict was still pending while MEMORY.md (by 10:19) already recorded READY — both kept; READY is the verified end state. Final artifact: 564,589,207 B, sha256 9ecd79461f646c84838f697488ebf46d900bf5dd1cfde2b9967db3f6f426d165; published into wbic16/rfcbox@exo (setup.sh reassembles and SHA-256-verifies); mirror on free-fall; SQ on logos-prime, API key required. Remainder: util-linux/libuuid license re-confirmation (pre-composition item); Lean instance-proof leg a named follow-on.
