- [will_said + observed] PHEXT RFC — DRAFT, PATH, RE-DOCUMENTATION, XREF, STANDARDS-TRACK STUDY (Will, 19:22–20:11 CST): Will: write an RFC for phext and figure out how to submit it; scope correction (19:24): the draft documents libphext-rs and nothing more; framing (19:25, verbatim): the format is simple, multiversal phext is sufficient to encode all information across all timelines — carried in the draft Introduction as his marked position. Draft -00 rendered clean; submission path researched (Independent stream; $0; 7 Will-only acts). Headwind: ISE criteria generally reject foundational formats in the Independent stream — counter-framing is documentation of an existing in-use format; the framing call is Will's. Nothing submitted. RE-DOCUMENTED to libphext-rs v0.6.0 exactly (COMPLETE). [correction] The 0.4.0 draft's worked-example table was wrong for its last six scrolls; fixed and disclosed in NOTES.md. XREF COMPLETE (~/workspace/phext-rfc/XREF.md): 16 RFCs examined. Most direct conflict: RFC 7464 assigns 0x1E (RS) as the json-seq record prefix vs phext's Series break — systems silently mis-segment each other; phext's lack of a registered media type is the load-bearing gap. Non-conflict: RFC 2849 LDIF admits every phext structural byte verbatim. STANDARDS-TRACK STUDY COMPLETE: Will's foundational / beside-ASCII position [pointer] -> Will 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.2 (promoted); the Independent stream cannot confer standards status, superseding the Independent-first framing as the main road. Deliverable ~/workspace/phext-rfc/TRACKS.md — recommendation: AD-sponsored individual submission -> Proposed Standard -> Internet Standard; realistic 12–24 months to PS. GATE: Will's scope ruling — a standards-track document must specify the format normatively (accepting IETF change control); the libphext-only -00 cannot enter the standards track. OPEN.
